   118	## 4. Clean Architecture Pattern
   119	
   120	### Scope
   121	- Label: `Hybrid`
   122	- Stack context: Python packages under `engine/packages/` and `neuron/packages/`
   123	
   124	### Decision
   125	- Layer boundaries: `brain_domain` (frozen dataclasses, enums, invariants, no I/O) → application packages (`brain_security`, `brain_temporal`, `brain_review`, `brain_content` ports) → infrastructure adapters (`brain_persistence`, local filesystem content adapter) → `brain_api` and `brain_worker`.
   126	- Dependency direction: inward only; adapters implement `Protocol` ports declared in application packages; `brain_api` wires them in `create_app()`.
   127	- `neuron/` mirrors the split: `brain_interpretation` (models, ports) → `brain_ingestion` (bundle writer and durable publication callback) and `brain_extraction` (the pipeline-neutral extraction port, the direct-baseline adapter, and result/evidence mapping). ADR-0060's Docling-Graph target was Rejected on 2026-11-08. Keep any pipeline-specific IDs and output directories outside domain contracts.
   128	
   129	### Rationale
   130	- Master blueprint section 114.3 (package list as code boundaries); BLUEPRINT 2.3 boundary rules.
   131	
   132	### Applied In
   133	- `engine/`: as above
   134	- `neuron/`: as above; writes to canonical truth only through engine commit services (section 64)
   135	
   136	### Enforcement Level
   137	- `MUST`
   138	
   139	### Example
   140	
   141	```text
   142	brain_domain -> brain_temporal (port: CanonicalFactRepository) -> brain_persistence (SQLAlchemy) -> brain_api
   143	```
   144	
   145	---
