   175	## 6. Data Modeling Pattern
   176	
   177	### Scope
   178	- Label: `Hybrid`
   179	- Stack context: PostgreSQL 18, SQLAlchemy 2, Alembic, range types with btree_gist
   180	
   181	### Decision
   182	- Entity identity strategy: UUID primary keys; external identifiers scoped by namespace and version (section 107.3); every authoritative row carries `tenant_id` and `knowledge_base_id` (ADR-0030).
   183	- Soft delete policy: canonical facts are never deleted or soft-deleted; they end with a change reason (ADR-0009); governed retention and deletion arrive with F0026 (proposed ADR-0043).
   184	- Temporal/audit fields: canonical fact and relationship versions carry `valid tstzrange` and `recorded tstzrange` with a two-range GiST exclusion; `source_received_at`, `artifact_created_at`, `assertion_created_at`, `canonical_accepted_at` are stored separately; all rows carry `created_at`.
   185	
   186	### Rationale
   187	- Sections 13 to 16, 78, 109.1, 109.2; ADR-0006 to ADR-0009.
   188	
   189	### Applied In
   190	- Entity model docs: `planning-mds/architecture/data-model.md`
   191	- Migrations: `engine/migrations/versions/`
   192	
   193	### Enforcement Level
   194	- `MUST`
   195	
   196	### Example
   197	
   198	```sql
   199	canonical_fact_version(id, slot_id, tenant_id, knowledge_base_id, value jsonb, valid tstzrange, recorded tstzrange, change_reason, commit_id,
   200	  EXCLUDE USING gist (slot_id WITH =, valid WITH &&, recorded WITH &&))
   201	```
   202	
