   205	## 7. Testing Pattern
   206	
   207	### Scope
   208	- Label: `Hybrid`
   209	- Stack context: pytest with coverage for `engine/` and `neuron/`; Playwright for `experience/` (from F0021)
   210	
   211	### Decision
   212	- Unit/integration/e2e split: unit tests own domain invariants and pure logic; integration tests run against the Compose stack (database, object store, authentik); evaluation tests run against the Golden Corpus fixtures; contract tests validate JSON Schemas and the OpenAPI document.
   213	- Coverage targets: 80% line coverage per workspace (framework evidence contract); severe-error rate and precision/recall reported with sample sizes (section 115.2).
   214	- Test data policy: synthetic or licensed fixtures only; no production documents; fixture text never enters telemetry.
   215	
   216	### Rationale
   217	- Sections 96 to 98, 115; framework feature evidence contract.
   218	
   219	### Applied In
   220	- Test plans: per feature under the run's `test-plan.md`
   460	
   461	New table UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE are denied, and populated downgrade refuses under table locks. Existing canonical version rows retain ADR-0078 close-only immutability. The lineage reader is derived/on-demand and has no authoritative graph/cache table. Existing F0018 RLS/DB-role and F0041 learning ownership remain unchanged.
   462	
   463	```mermaid
   464	erDiagram
   465	    REVIEW_DECISION ||--o| LEARNING_CANDIDATE_RESERVATION : effective_correction
   466	    ASSERTION ||--o| LEARNING_CANDIDATE_RESERVATION : corrected_child
   467	    REVIEW_ITEM ||--o{ REVIEW_SUBMISSION_ATTEMPT : non_applied
   468	    ASSERTION ||--o{ REVIEW_SUBMISSION_ATTEMPT : original_claim
   469	```
   470	
   471	## F0021 browser sessions and throttle (Phase B design 2026-11-27, proposed ADR-0082)
   472	
   473	Migration 0018 (design: [migration-design.sql](../features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/migration-design.sql)) is expand-only.
   474	
   475	**`browser_login_attempt`:** one row per sign-in started.
   476	
   477	- Stores only digests of the state, browser binding and nonce, plus the encrypted PKCE verifier.
   478	- Holds the mode (`redirect` or `popup`, with a popup reference) and the sanitized return route.
   479	- Expires after 10 minutes and can be consumed once.
   480	
   481	**`browser_session`:** the server-side session behind the opaque cookie.
   482	
   483	- Keyed by a UUID session reference. Only the cookie's SHA-256 digest is stored.
   484	- Holds the principal, issuer, subject and display name.
   485	- Holds the idle deadline (30 min), absolute deadline (8 h) and access-token expiry.
   486	- Tokens are an AES-256-GCM ciphertext under a key ID; ending a session sets it to NULL.
   487	- Also holds the renewal count, CSRF digest, active tenant/knowledge base (composite FK to `knowledge_base(id, tenant_id)`) and the end reason.
   488	- CHECKs tie together:
   489	  - lifetime and D1;
   490	  - ended state and token absence;
   491	  - the active pair.
   492	
   493	**`session_event`:** append-only session lifecycle audit, using the migration 0007 trigger.
   494	
   495	- Records creation, replacement, renewal and its failure, idle and absolute endings, and principal endings.
   496	- Records logout, with the revocation and end-session outcomes.
   497	- Records active knowledge-base changes.
   498	
   499	**`credential_rejection_window`:** mutable per-client counters for 60-second windows. One atomic upsert per rejected credential; rows older than 10 minutes are pruned.
   500	
   501	**Display names:** `tenant.display_name` and `knowledge_base.display_name` are nullable, server-owned names for the shell.
   502	
   503	Rejected credentials keep using `authentication_event`, with twelve new reason codes and an optional payload (session reference, CSRF cause, client key for `rate_limited`). Authorization never reads session state: the active knowledge base narrows shell requests only.
